                <a href="#phase2" style="color: var(--nav-text); text-decoration: none; padding: 4px 8px; border-radius: 3px; background-color: var(--nav-bg); display: inline-block;">Phase 2</a>
                <a href="#phase3" style="color: var(--nav-text); text-decoration: none; padding: 4px 8px; border-radius: 3px; background-color: var(--nav-bg); display: inline-block;">Phase 3</a>
                <a href="#verification" style="color: var(--nav-text); text-decoration: none; padding: 4px 8px; border-radius: 3px; background-color: var(--nav-bg); display: inline-block;">Verification</a>
                <a href="#out-of-scope" style="color: var(--nav-text); text-decoration: none; padding: 4px 8px; border-radius: 3px; background-color: var(--nav-bg); display: inline-block;">Out of Scope</a>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- OVERVIEW SECTION -->
    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="overview" style="color: var(--text-color); font-family: var(--header-font);">1. Overview</h2>
            <p style="color: var(--text-color); font-family: var(--body-font);"><strong>Why:</strong> The Zenflow service priced itself out ~a month ago. Its worktree registry is hardcoded in two places that drift independently and most of its checkouts are already gone from disk (only <code>aichatsystem-ef4e</code> survives; the <code>ai</code> branch exists but was never in the registry). The AI2 editor's Review &amp; Merge panel (built last session) calls <code>/admin/git/worktrees</code> / <code>review</code> / <code>test_gate</code> / <code>merge_to_main</code> / <code>push_main</code> — all of which exist — but the <em>creation</em> half of "isolate AI code creation" is missing. This plan stands that up on a self-hosted directory with one source of truth.</p>
            <p style="text-align: right; margin-top: var(--spacing-small);"><a href="#toc" style="color: var(--link-color); font-size: var(--font-size-small);">↑ Back to Top</a></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- DECISIONS SECTION -->
    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="decisions" style="color: var(--text-color); font-family: var(--header-font);">2. Decisions (locked with user)</h2>
            <ul style="color: var(--text-color); font-family: var(--body-font);">
                <li><strong>Base dir:</strong> <code>~/.comserv/worktrees/</code> (matches the <code>~/.comserv/secrets</code> convention; names the <em>system</em>, not a feature).</li>
                <li><strong>Single source of truth:</strong> <code>root/config/worktrees.json</code> — read by both <code>Util::Git</code> and the planning tab. Kills the drift bug.</li>
                <li><strong>Initial branches:</strong> only <code>ai</code> + <code>aichatsystem-ef4e</code> get a checkout + port. All other former zenflow entries are retired (their checkouts are already gone).</li>
                <li><strong>main:</strong> unchanged. The primary repo checkout at <code>/home/shanta/PycharmProjects/comserv2/Comserv</code> stays on port 3001.</li>
            </ul>
            <p style="text-align: right; margin-top: var(--spacing-small);"><a href="#toc" style="color: var(--link-color); font-size: var(--font-size-small);">↑ Back to Top</a></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- INVENTORY SECTION -->
    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="inventory" style="color: var(--text-color); font-family: var(--header-font);">3. Inventory of what the old system touches (must migrate)</h2>
            <table style="border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;font-size:0.9em;">
                <tr style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border-color);">
                    <th style="text-align:left;padding:4px 8px;color:var(--text-color);">File</th>
                    <th style="text-align:left;padding:4px 8px;color:var(--text-color);">Hardcoded zenflow reference</th>
                </tr>
                <tr style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border-color);"><td style="padding:4px 8px;color:var(--text-color);"><code>lib/Comserv/Util/Git.pm</code></td><td style="padding:4px 8px;color:var(--text-color);"><code>WORKTREE_PORTS</code> hash + <code>_worktree_row</code> regex <code>\.zenflow/worktrees/</code> + <code>run_test_gate</code> path <code>$HOME/.zenflow/worktrees/$branch/Comserv</code></td></tr>
                <tr style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border-color);"><td style="padding:4px 8px;color:var(--text-color);"><code>root/admin/planning/_planning_tab.tt</code></td><td style="padding:4px 8px;color:var(--text-color);"><code>bp</code> + <code>all_branches</code> static maps (duplicate of the above) + literal <code>cd ~/.zenflow/worktrees/&lt;branch&gt;/Comserv &amp;&amp; perl ... -p &lt;port&gt;</code></td></tr>
                <tr style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border-color);"><td style="padding:4px 8px;color:var(--text-color);"><code>lib/Comserv/Controller/Root.pm</code></td><td style="padding:4px 8px;color:var(--text-color);"><code>IS_DEV_WORKTREE</code> constant regex <code>\.zenflow[/\\]worktrees[/\\]</code> → stashes <code>is_dev_server</code></td></tr>
                <tr style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border-color);"><td style="padding:4px 8px;color:var(--text-color);"><code>lib/Comserv/Util/SystemInfo.pm</code></td><td style="padding:4px 8px;color:var(--text-color);"><code>get_app_workflow</code> regex <code>/\.zenflow/worktrees/([^/]+)</code> → drives <code>app_workflow</code> stash + planning "currently on branch"</td></tr>
                <tr style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border-color);"><td style="padding:4px 8px;color:var(--text-color);"><code>lib/Comserv/Controller/Admin/Git.pm</code></td><td style="padding:4px 8px;color:var(--text-color);"><code>worktree_list</code> uses <code>list_worktrees</code> (porcelain parse; path-agnostic) — OK to keep, but port lookup must move to the JSON.</td></tr>
            </table>
            <p style="text-align: right; margin-top: var(--spacing-small);"><a href="#toc" style="color: var(--link-color); font-size: var(--font-size-small);">↑ Back to Top</a></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- DATA CONTRACT SECTION -->
    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="contract" style="color: var(--text-color); font-family: var(--header-font);">4. New data contract — <code>root/config/worktrees.json</code></h2>
            <pre style="background:#1e1f22;color:#9cdcfe;padding:10px;border-radius:4px;overflow:auto;"><code>{
  "base_dir": "/home/shanta/.comserv/worktrees",
  "port_start": 4001,
  "branches": {
    "ai":                { "port": 4001, "label": "AIChat",          "url": "/planning/daily" },
    "aichatsystem-ef4e": { "port": 4010, "label": "AIChatSystem",    "url": "/planning/daily" }
  }
}</code></pre>
            <p style="color: var(--text-color); font-family: var(--body-font);">Rules: <code>base_dir</code> is absolute (expand <code>~</code> at load). <code>main</code> is never listed here (it is the primary checkout, port 3001). <code>create_worktree</code> appends a key with the next free port. A worktree path is always <code>&lt;base_dir&gt;/&lt;branch&gt;/Comserv</code>.</p>
            <p style="text-align: right; margin-top: var(--spacing-small);"><a href="#toc" style="color: var(--link-color); font-size: var(--font-size-small);">↑ Back to Top</a></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- PHASE 0 -->
    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="phase0" style="color: var(--text-color); font-family: var(--header-font);">5. Phase 0 — Infra / config (do this first, gate before any app code)</h2>
            <ol style="color: var(--text-color); font-family: var(--body-font);">
                <li>Create <code>root/config/worktrees.json</code> with the contract above.</li>
                <li>Create the base dir and migrate the two live checkouts:
                    <ul>
                        <li><code>mkdir -p ~/.comserv/worktrees</code></li>
                        <li><code>git worktree add ~/.comserv/worktrees/ai/Comserv ai</code></li>
                        <li><code>git worktree add ~/.comserv/worktrees/aichatsystem-ef4e/Comserv aichatsystem-ef4e</code></li>
                        <li>Remove the stale zenflow checkouts: <code>git worktree remove ~/.zenflow/worktrees/aichatsystem-ef4e --force</code> and drop the <code>~/.zenflow/worktrees</code> tree once nothing references it.</li>
                    </ul>
                </li>
                <li>Verify the old <code>~/.zenflow</code> entries are fully unreferenced after Phase 2 (no remaining <code>.zenflow</code> string in code).</li>
            </ol>
            <p style="text-align: right; margin-top: var(--spacing-small);"><a href="#toc" style="color: var(--link-color); font-size: var(--font-size-small);">↑ Back to Top</a></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- PHASE 1 -->
    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="phase1" style="color: var(--text-color); font-family: var(--header-font);">6. Phase 1 — Single source of truth in Perl</h2>
            <ol style="color: var(--text-color); font-family: var(--body-font);">
                <li><code>Util::Git</code>: add <code>load_worktree_config($c)</code> (read + cache <code>worktrees.json</code>, expand <code>~</code>). Replace <code>WORKTREE_PORTS</code> usage:
                    <ul>
                        <li><code>_worktree_row</code>: detect a worktree by <code>base_dir</code> instead of the <code>.zenflow</code> regex; port from the JSON (fallback <code>0</code>).</li>
                        <li><code>run_test_gate</code>: derive <code>$wt_dir</code> from <code>base_dir/branch/Comserv</code>; keep the existing <code>script/test_gate.sh --fast</code> invocation.</li>
                    </ul>
                </li>
                <li><code>Root.pm</code>: change <code>IS_DEV_WORKTREE</code> to match <code>base_dir</code> (<code>\.comserv[/\\]worktrees[/\\]</code>).</li>
                <li><code>SystemInfo-&gt;get_app_workflow</code>: change the regex to <code>/\.comserv/worktrees/([^/]+)</code>.</li>
                <li>Keep <code>WORKTREE_PORTS</code> only as an internal fallback if JSON is missing; prefer the JSON.</li>
            </ol>
            <p style="text-align: right; margin-top: var(--spacing-small);"><a href="#toc" style="color: var(--link-color); font-size: var(--font-size-small);">↑ Back to Top</a></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- PHASE 2 -->
    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="phase2" style="color: var(--text-color); font-family: var(--header-font);">7. Phase 2 — Planning tab reads the JSON (kill the duplicate)</h2>
            <ol style="color: var(--text-color); font-family: var(--body-font);">
                <li>Controller feeding <code>_planning_tab.tt</code> (Documentation.pm <code>daily_plan</code> / Planning.pm) stashes <code>worktree_list</code> derived from <code>load_worktree_config</code> (name, port, label, url, and the launch <code>cmd</code> built from <code>base_dir</code>).</li>
                <li><code>_planning_tab.tt</code>: replace the static <code>bp</code> + <code>all_branches</code> maps with a FOREACH over the stashed list. "Start command" becomes <code>cd &lt;base_dir&gt;/&lt;branch&gt;/Comserv &amp;&amp; CATALYST_DEBUG=1 COMSERV_NO_HEALTH_LOG=1 perl script/comserv_server.pl -p &lt;port&gt; -r</code>.</li>
                <li>No inline <code>&lt;script&gt;</code> added here; existing <code>smartOpenBranch</code>/<code>branchAction</code> JS stays.</li>
            </ol>
            <p style="text-align: right; margin-top: var(--spacing-small);"><a href="#toc" style="color: var(--link-color); font-size: var(--font-size-small);">↑ Back to Top</a></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- PHASE 3 -->
    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="phase3" style="color: var(--text-color); font-family: var(--header-font);">8. Phase 3 — create_worktree (the isolation primitive)</h2>
            <ol style="color: var(--text-color); font-family: var(--body-font);">
                <li><code>Util::Git-&gt;create_worktree($c, $branch, $opts)</code>: pick next free port (max existing +1, or <code>port_start</code>), <code>git worktree add &lt;base_dir&gt;/&lt;branch&gt;/Comserv &lt;branch&gt;</code> (create branch from <code>main</code> if it does not exist), append the key to <code>worktrees.json</code>.</li>
                <li><code>Admin/Git</code>: <code>POST /admin/git/create_worktree</code> (admin-gated) → returns <code>{branch, port, path, cmd}</code>. Used by the AI2 editor to spin up an isolated checkout on demand.</li>
                <li>Optional follow-up (separate plan): a one-click "launch instance" from the planning tab using the returned <code>cmd</code>.</li>
            </ol>
            <p style="text-align: right; margin-top: var(--spacing-small);"><a href="#toc" style="color: var(--link-color); font-size: var(--font-size-small);">↑ Back to Top</a></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- VERIFICATION SECTION -->
    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="verification" style="color: var(--text-color); font-family: var(--header-font);">9. Verification</h2>
            <ul style="color: var(--text-color); font-family: var(--body-font);">
                <li><code>perl -c</code> on every modified <code>.pm</code>.</li>
                <li><code>GET /admin/git/worktrees</code> on 3001 now returns <code>ai</code> + <code>aichatsystem-ef4e</code> with ports 4001/4010 and <code>is_main:0</code>; <code>main</code> flagged <code>is_main:1</code>.</li>
                <li>Planning tab dropdown lists exactly the two branches; "currently on" reflects the running worktree via <code>app_workflow</code>.</li>
                <li><code>grep -rn "zenflow" lib/ root/</code> returns nothing after Phase 2.</li>
                <li>AI2 editor Review panel loads the diff/test-gate/merge against the new paths.</li>
            </ul>
            <p style="text-align: right; margin-top: var(--spacing-small);"><a href="#toc" style="color: var(--link-color); font-size: var(--font-size-small);">↑ Back to Top</a></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- OUT OF SCOPE SECTION -->
    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <div id="out-of-scope" class="success" style="background-color: rgba(255,255,255,0.15); border-left: 4px solid var(--success-color); padding: var(--spacing-medium); border-radius: 4px; margin: var(--spacing-medium) 0;">
                <h2 style="color: var(--success-color); font-family: var(--header-font); margin-top: 0;">10. Out of scope (call out, don't do)</h2>
                <ul style="color: var(--text-color); font-family: var(--body-font);">
                    <li>DB isolation for worktree app instances (separate <a href="/Documentation/dev_isolation_and_backups_plan" style="color: var(--link-color);">dev_isolation_and_backups_plan</a> concern).</li>
                    <li>Re-registering the 25+ dead former zenflow branches.</li>
                    <li>Any change to the primary <code>main</code> checkout or port 3001.</li>
                </ul>
            </div>
            <p style="text-align: right; margin-top: var(--spacing-small);"><a href="#toc" style="color: var(--link-color); font-size: var(--font-size-small);">↑ Back to Top</a></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- FOOTER SECTION -->
    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <div style="margin-top: var(--spacing-large); padding-top: var(--spacing-medium); border-top: 1px solid var(--border-color); color: var(--text-muted-color); font-size: var(--font-size-small);">
